am-mckinley-park","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"William McKinley Park","title":"Saturday: Circle McKinley Park","subtitle":"Pair the jogging path with the rose garden and pond","notes":"Follow one circuit of the mapped jogging path, pause at the rose garden, and use only designated pedestrian areas.","short_summary":"Shift from Midtown activity to a mapped neighborhood green space.","evidence_claim":"The City of Sacramento’s official McKinley Park map identifies a jogging path, rose garden, lake, tennis courts, picnic areas, and restrooms at 3330 McKinley Boulevard.","source_url":"https://www.cityofsacramento.gov/content/dam/portal/ypce/Parks/mckinley_map-10-2022.pdf","source_title":"McKinley Park Map","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor amenities are mapped by the city. Organized use and reservations may carry fees; follow posted park rules and closures.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"california-state-capitol-park","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"California State Capitol Park","title":"Saturday: Read the Memorials in Capitol Park","subtitle":"Explore the grounds while the Capitol building is closed","notes":"Stay outdoors, locate two named memorials on the grounds, and read their inscriptions rather than expecting a weekend building tour.","short_summary":"Approach California civic history through the Capitol grounds.","evidence_claim":"California State Parks places the Capitol Museum and Capitol Park at 10th and L streets and identifies memorials on the grounds; the Capitol building is closed on weekends.","source_url":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?lang=en&page_id=495","source_title":"California State Capitol Museum","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The Capitol building